{"id":"maillart-fleming-1935","title":"Maillart & Fleming: Peking to Kashmir","who":"Ella Maillart and Peter Fleming","when":"February–September 1935","vehicle":"Train, lorry, horse, camel and on foot","kind":"other","color":"#a16207","media":[{"kind":"book","title":"Forbidden Journey","by":"Ella Maillart"},{"kind":"book","title":"News from Tartary","by":"Peter Fleming"}],"summary":"A Swiss sailor-skier and a Times correspondent cross China from Peking to Srinagar, 3,500 miles in seven months, to see what was happening in closed Xinjiang after the Kumul rebellion. Deserts, the Tsaidam marshes, caravans and Himalayan passes; two books of the same journey that read very differently.","sources":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Ella Maillart","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ella_Maillart"},{"label":"Wikipedia: News from Tartary","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/News_from_Tartary"},{"label":"Papers Past: Fleming's own report (Evening Post, Dec 1935)","url":"https://paperspast.natlib.govt.nz/newspapers/EP19351202.2.54"}],"approximate":"Main towns of the journey; the tracks across the deserts are drawn as straight lines.","km":5512,"bbox":[73.0895,31.5905,116.3913,39.9057],"stops":[{"name":"Peking","place":"Beijing, China","at":[39.9057,116.3913],"date":"16 Feb 1935","text":"They set off together, against all advice.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Skyline_of_Beijing_CBD_with_B-5906_approaching_%2820211016171955%29_%281%29.jpg/500px-Skyline_of_Beijing_CBD_with_B-5906_approaching_%2820211016171955%29_%281%29.jpg","page":"Beijing","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Skyline_of_Beijing_CBD_with_B-5906_approaching_%2820211016171955%29_%281%29.jpg","credit":"N509FZ","license":"CC BY 4.0"}},{"name":"Lanchow","place":"Lanzhou, China","at":[36.2859,103.6323],"text":"By train and lorry into the northwest.","by":"train","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Skyline_Lanzhou_August_2025.jpg/500p